<section class=3D"segment seg1" id=3D"seg1">
  <div class=3D"seg-label">Segment 1 =E2=80=94 The Hook</div>
  <h2>Triple Whale Launches Moby 2 =E2=80=94 "The AI Operating System for E=
commerce"</h2>
  <p class=3D"seg-reason">Why lead with this: Announced May 19 =E2=80=94 mo=
st time-sensitive story. 60K DTC brands already on TW. The "AI replaces you=
r marketing team" narrative is the biggest conversation in DTC right now. <=
span class=3D"time-flag">Cover Now</span></p>

  <div class=3D"sub-heading">Setup (Why Listeners Should Care)</div>
  <p>Triple Whale just went from analytics dashboard to "AI operating syste=
m for ecommerce." Moby 2 launched May 19 with autonomous ad management, cre=
ative generation, landing page building, inventory forecasting, and custome=
r segmentation. Copilot mode (you approve) or Autopilot mode (it runs). Thr=
ee upcoming "Moby Specialists": Media Buyer (owns ROAS), Creative Director =
(owns CTR), Conversion Optimizer (owns conversion rate). Credit-based prici=
ng. Multi-model orchestration across Claude, GPT, and Gemini. 60K+ brands, =
$82B+ GMV feeding the system.</p>

  <div class=3D"sub-heading">Talking Points</div>
  <ol class=3D"talking-points">
    <li><strong>The positioning shift is massive.</strong> TW isn't competi=
ng with Northbeam/Rockerbox anymore =E2=80=94 they're trying to replace you=
r media buyer, creative strategist, and CRO team. That's a fundamentally di=
fferent value prop and buyer conversation.</li>
    <li><strong>Credit-based pricing is telling.</strong> Revenue scales wi=
th how much work Moby does. If it actually replaces human work, TW captures=
 a % of that labor cost. Aligns incentives=E2=80=A6 or creates a perverse i=
ncentive to burn credits.</li>
    <li><strong>The "Context Engine" underneath</strong> =E2=80=94 persiste=
nt memory, knowledge graph per account, expert-built playbooks baked in. Th=
is is what separates it from "I pasted my data into ChatGPT."</li>
    <li><strong>The data moat:</strong> 60K brands and $82B+ GMV means the =
benchmarks and playbooks get better for everyone. Network effect most marte=
ch can't replicate.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class=3D"sub-heading">User Feedback to Reference</div>
  <div class=3D"feedback-block fb-bull">
    <div class=3D"fb-label">Bull</div>
    <p>True Classic CEO says Moby 2 "optimizes against business outcomes, n=
ot platform metrics." One operator canceled analyst hires after testing Mob=
y Agents.</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"feedback-block fb-bear">
    <div class=3D"fb-label">Bear</div>
    <p>140+ tracked attribution outages since 2024. G2 reviews: "delivers w=
rong data" with offline/marketplace orders misattributed. Trustpilot: "Sinc=
e day one, the data has been inaccurate."</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"feedback-block fb-mid">
    <div class=3D"fb-label">Middle Ground</div>
    <p>ATTN Agency (40+ DTC accounts, 3 years): 8.2/10 overall. "Some brand=
s swear by it, others churned after a quarter." Moby AI "most useful for qu=
ick forecasting and anomaly detection rather than creative generation, wher=
e human judgment still wins."</p>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"tension">
    <div class=3D"tension-label">The Tension / Debate Angle</div>
    <p>TW is asking brands to let an AI agent autonomously manage their ad =
spend, but the platform has 140+ documented attribution outages. They're bu=
ilding the most ambitious AI execution layer in ecommerce on top of a data =
foundation users have publicly questioned. If Moby 2's autonomous actions a=
re powered by the same attribution engine that's been unreliable, how much =
do you trust autopilot mode?</p>
    <p><strong>For agencies:</strong> If Moby Media Buyer manages bids and =
budgets across Meta and Google, backed by first-party data from 60K brands =
=E2=80=94 what exactly is the performance marketing agency's role? TW is bu=
ilding the AI replacement for $10-20K/month agency retainers.</p>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"questions">
    <div class=3D"q-label">Questions to Bounce</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Would you put your ad account on Moby autopilot? Why or why not?<=
/li>
      <li>Is "AI operating system" the right framing, or is this an attribu=
tion company cosplaying as an execution platform?</li>
      <li>What happens when Moby pauses your best ad set at 2am because its=
 model detected a ROAS dip that was actually a tracking lag?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

